To generate the assert statement for the given comment, we need to express the condition that for every valid index from the given `index` to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either `null` and the old element at this index is `null`, or the element at the next position equals the old element at this index.

Here's the assert statement in the required format:

<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i));</code>

This assert statement ensures that for every index `i` from `index` to the old size of the list minus one, the element at position `i+1` is either `null` and the element at position `i` was `null`, or the element at position `i+1` is the same as the element at position `i` before the insertion.
